<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baalis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 580 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baalis was a king of Ammon in the early 6th century BCE, after the Babylonian destruction of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-jeremiah">Book of Jeremiah</a> says he sent Ishmael son of Nethaniah to murder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gedaliah">Gedaliah</a>, the governor appointed over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a>. A seal impression naming a servant of 'Baalyasha, king of the Ammonites', found at Tell el-Umeiri, is often linked with him.</p></div>
